        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(core): surface non_deliverable_terminal_turn as outbound fallback to channel plugins",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes #102113\n\nWhen `resolveAttemptTrajectoryTerminal()` classifies a run as `non_deliverable_terminal_turn` (e.g. `stopReason=toolUse` with no committed delivery evidence, or no visible output produced), the `terminalError` field was written only to the trajectory recorder and never propagated to `EmbeddedAgentRunResult.meta`. As a result:\n\n- `agent-runner-execution.ts` never set `terminalRunFailed=true` for this case\n- `followup-runner.ts` built no fallback payload\n- `message_tool_only` channels (e.g. openclaw-channel-octo) received nothing and went completely silent\n\n## Root Cause\n\n`attempt-trajectory-status.ts` sets `terminalError: NON_DELIVERABLE_TERMINAL_TURN_REASON` on the `AttemptTrajectoryTerminal` object, but `attempt.ts` only forwarded this field to the trajectory recorder — **not to the returned attempt object**. Consequently, `EmbeddedAgentRunMeta` had no way to signal this condition downstream.\n\nIn `agent-runner-execution.ts`, the `else if (deferredLifecycleError || embeddedError)` guard only fires on `meta.error` (which tracks a different error kind). `non_deliverable_terminal_turn` was invisible there.\n\nIn `followup-runner.ts`, even when `terminalRunFailed=true`, the `run.sourceReplyDeliveryMode !== \"message_tool_only\"` guard blocks the fallback for channels that use message tool as their sole delivery path — which is exactly the case for Octo.\n\n## Fix (5 files, +17/-3)\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `types.ts` | Add `nonDeliverableTerminalTurn?: true` to `EmbeddedAgentRunMeta` |\n| `attempt.ts` | Expose the flag in the attempt return value |\n| `run.ts` | Pass it through to `meta` in the normal terminal return path |\n| `agent-runner-execution.ts` | Read `meta.nonDeliverableTerminalTurn` → set `terminalRunFailed=true` + supply user-facing fallback text `\"The agent run failed before producing a reply.\"` |\n| `followup-runner.ts` | Allow `message_tool_only` mode to still deliver the terminal failure payload when `nonDeliverableTerminalTurn` is true |\n\n## Path Reachability\n\n```\nresolveAttemptTrajectoryTerminal()           // attempt-trajectory-status.ts:103\n  └─ stopReason=toolUse + no delivery evidence\n       → terminalError: NON_DELIVERABLE_TERMINAL_TURN_REASON  // :131\n\nrunEmbeddedAttempt() return                  // attempt.ts:5957 (new)\n  └─ nonDeliverableTerminalTurn: true\n\nrunEmbeddedAgentInternal() meta              // run.ts:4258 (new)\n  └─ meta.nonDeliverableTerminalTurn: true\n\nrunAgentTurnWithFallbackInternal()           // agent-runner-execution.ts:3242 (new)\n  └─ else if (...|| meta.nonDeliverableTerminalTurn)\n       → terminalRunFailed = true\n       → terminalErrorMessage = \"The agent run failed before producing a reply.\"\n\ncreateFollowupRunner()                       // followup-runner.ts:1567 (new)\n  └─ (sourceReplyDeliveryMode !== \"message_tool_only\"\n      || meta.nonDeliverableTerminalTurn)    // bypass message_tool_only gate\n       → buildTerminalAgentRunFailureReplyPayload(...)\n       → fallback delivered to channel\n```\n\n## Reproduction\n\nTrigger: Octo agent turn where `stopReason=toolUse` and delivery evidence is not committed (message tool call completes but `hasCommittedOutboundDeliveryEvidence` returns false). The user previously saw no response.\n\nExpected after fix: User receives `\"The agent run failed before producing a reply.\"`\n\n## Impact\n\n- All `message_tool_only` channels (Octo and others) now receive the fallback text on `non_deliverable_terminal_turn`\n- Non-`message_tool_only` channels: no behavior change (the `message_tool_only` guard was never reached for them)\n- Heartbeat runs: unaffected (`isInteractive=false` guard still fires first)\n- Silent runs (`silentExpected=true`): unaffected (guarded earlier in `buildEmptyInteractiveReplyPayload`)\n\n## Related\n\n- Issue: #102113\n- Channel-side tracking: Mininglamp-OSS/openclaw-channel-octo#150",
        "branch": "fix/102113-non-deliverable-terminal-turn-fallback",
